# inc-r6u1 (bounded probe): can a Glyph of Warding blast be driven in play, and
# does its combat message print the die COUNT the way Searing Light's does?
#
# The rune explodes via Terrain "strange rune"'s EV_SPECIAL (lib/wspells.irh),
# which calls ThrowTerraDmg(EV_DAMAGE, AD_NORM, EMap->GetTerraDmg(...), ...)
# (src/Event.cpp:733). GetTerraDmg rolls the stored Dice and returns a single
# integer, so ThrowTerraDmg receives a flat number -- there is no dice string
# to read. This script is the empirical confirmation of that reading: it casts
# Greater Glyph of Warding (pval (LEVEL_1PER2_MAX5)d8 / was (LEVEL_SCALED)d8)
# on the square east of the priest, steps onto it, and dumps the message log.
#
#   INCURSION_OPTIONS=tools/fixtures/options-2026-08-22.dat \
#   INCURSION_RUN_DIR="$PWD/logs/inc-r6u1/glyph-probe" \
#       tools/headless.sh tools/keys/glyph-warding-cap.keys 1
@include searing-light-cl11-setup.keys
w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Glyph of Warding, Greater" ENTER
m
@choose "Glyph of Warding, Greater"
RIGHT
ENTER
@dump:glyph-placed
RIGHT
@while "Confirm enter" y
@while "more --" SPACE
@dump:glyph-triggered
v
@dump:glyph-messages
@while "Messages" ESC
@quit
